Z||000013||RRobinson||09-22-2001||01:36 PM||||Here's mine...<P>1993-1994: 87 GT 5-Speed, Maroon...sold this basket case. <P>1994-present: 88 GT auto, Red, 40K.<P>1994-1995: 86 GT 5-speed, red, sold...regretted it. It had 40K as well. Nice one.<P>1996-present: 87 GT 5s, black, 56K.<P>1998-present: 87 GT Blue, 5s, 18K!<P>Jan 2001-present: 87 SE V6 Maroon, 5s, 111K.<P>June 2001-present: 86 GT 5s, Red...carbon copy of the one I had in mid 90's. 42K.<P>July 2001-present: 88 GT 5s: 5.5K, Red, lumbar seats, sunroof, wing etc. Mint.<P>Still on the lookout for a nice low mileage Formula or Indy...<P>RR<BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by RRobinson (edited 09-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||mrfiero||09-22-2001||04:43 PM||||OK......here I go:<P>#1 black '88 GT (my first one, bought April 1990....wrecked in Dec. '95)<P>#2 red '88 Formula T-Top (sold to kid in MN)<P>#3 silver '85 SE T-Top (sold)<P>#4 burgundy '88 Formula (sold to friend, later wrecked)<P>#5 white '88 Formula T-Top (sold to Ed Parks....he still has it in the showroom)<P>#6 black '88 GT (bought in 1997 with 10K miles......still have, now with 16K miles)<P>#7 '88 Formula yellow (sold to guy in OH)<P>#8 black '88 GT (sold to guy in MI)<P>#9 silver '88 GT (sold to a local guy)<P>#10 silver '88 Formula (less than 300 orig. miles, sold to guy in AL) <P>#11 burgundy '88 GT T-Top (current daily driver.<P>I forgot one! <P>#12 burgundy '87 coupe.  This one was pieced together by Jeremy (works at Fiero Factory) when my turbocharged quad 4 '85 GT died.  He bought the GT and gave me this coupe so I could get home after I left the Fiero factory in Jan. '99.  I sold to a guy a few months later and he promptly wrecked it.  It was the ugliest Fiero I have ever owned, but surprisingly it was the best driver (had '88 coupe engine & auto tranny)......go figure.<P>I think that is it.  I know I have owned 50-60 Fieros, but the majority were parts cars or were immediately sold after acquiring.<P>All told, since April 1990 I have driven over 350,000 miles (most of it trouble free) on my 11 Fieros.  Who says they're not reliable?<P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||10
